index 0000000..74bd25a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/website-project-preview-release-tag.md
@@ -0,0 +1,124 @@
+# Website project preview: release-tag pinning (GIT-001C pin-drift fix)
+
+Status: candidate procedure. Nothing here has been executed.
+
+## Problem this solves
+
+Before this change the build workflow was dispatched on `main`, while the
+source-token, artifact and completion endpoints require one exact, reviewed
+workflow commit (`LWS_PREVIEW_WORKFLOW_SHA`, `LWS_PREVIEW_COMPLETION_WORKFLOW_SHA`
+and the database allowlist). Every later commit on `main`, including
+documentation, made GitHub run a different commit than the pin. The OIDC broker
+then correctly refused with `OIDC_WORKFLOW_REVISION_MISMATCH`, which the
+source-token handler masked as `503 SOURCE_TOKEN_EXCHANGE_FAILED`.
+The `workflow_run` completion monitor always runs from the default branch and
+drifted the same way.
+
+## Design
+
+- **Build**: dispatched on a protected, lightweight tag
+  `lws-preview-runner-YYYYMMDD-NN`. GitHub then sets `ref`, `workflow_ref`,
+  `sha` and `workflow_sha` from the tag, so the run commit stays equal to the pin
+  while `main` moves.
+- **Completion**: `complete-website-project-preview.yml` on `main` is a thin
+  caller with no logic. It calls
+  `complete-website-project-preview-runner.yml` at the same tag. The completion
+  endpoint checks the caller's identity (repository, `refs/heads/main`,
+  `workflow_run`, run id, attempt 1) and pins the runner through the OIDC
+  claims `job_workflow_ref` and `job_workflow_sha`.
+- **Pre-dispatch guard**: before the dispatch POST the commit behind the
+  configured ref is read. A difference ends the attempt as
+  `PROJECT_PREVIEW_WORKFLOW_PIN_DRIFT`; an unreadable ref as
+  `PROJECT_PREVIEW_WORKFLOW_PIN_UNVERIFIABLE`. Both record `REJECTED`, so the
+  lease is released instead of left `ACCEPTED`.
+- **Diagnostics**: OIDC revision, attempt, event and job-workflow refusals are
+  returned as their own codes instead of a generic 503.
+- `refs/heads/main` stays accepted as legacy configuration, which allows a
+  configuration-only rollback.
+
+## Configuration per release (no secret values)
+
+With `T` = tag name and `M` = the reviewed 40-hex commit the tag points to:
+
+| Function | Variable | Value |
+|---|---|---|
+| commercial-operator-command | `LWS_PREVIEW_WORKFLOW_REF_NAME` | `refs/tags/T` |
+| commercial-operator-command | `LWS_PREVIEW_WORKFLOW_SHA` | `M` |
+| website-project-preview-source-token, website-project-preview-artifact | `LWS_PREVIEW_WORKFLOW_REF_NAME` | `refs/tags/T` |
+| website-project-preview-source-token, website-project-preview-artifact | `LWS_PREVIEW_WORKFLOW_REF` | `lorenzobombello-max/lorenzo-web-studio/.github/workflows/build-website-project-preview.yml@refs/tags/T` |
+| website-project-preview-completion | `LWS_PREVIEW_WORKFLOW_REF_NAME` | `refs/tags/T` |
+| website-project-preview-completion | `LWS_PREVIEW_COMPLETION_WORKFLOW_SHA` | `M` |
+| database | `lws_internal.website_project_preview_workflow_revisions` | `M` enabled |
+
+The caller file on `main` must name `T` in both `uses: ...@T` and
+`platform_ref: T` (enforced by `scripts/website-project-preview-workflow.test.mjs`).
+
+## Release order (each step needs separate owner approval)
+
+1. Stop new preview requests; let in-flight runs finish. Handle stale leases only
+   via their own approved procedure (for dossier 007: WP-A terminalisation).
+2. Merge the reviewed candidate to `main` as commit `M`. Its caller file already
+   names `T`. Until step 3 the caller cannot resolve the runner, so no build may
+   run in between.
+3. Create the lightweight tag `T` on `M` (not annotated: the guard requires
+   `object.type == "commit"`).
+4. Add a tag ruleset for `refs/tags/lws-preview-runner-*`: block update
+   (force-move) and deletion, and restrict creation to the owner.
+5. Set the variables above, add `M` to the allowlist, deploy the four functions,
+   then read the configuration back for equality without publishing secrets.
+6. Run exactly one approved acceptance build: dispatch on `T`, one run claim,
+   source token, build, upload, finalisation and completion.
+7. Only after a PASS, disable the old allowlist rows that are no longer used.
+
+A later release repeats this with a new tag (`...-NN+1`). Commits on `main`
+between releases no longer affect running previews.
+
+## Facts to prove on staging before production
+
+- Run-API `head_branch` for a run dispatched on a tag equals the tag name.
+- The `job_workflow_ref` of a reusable workflow called at a tag has the form
+  `owner/repo/.github/workflows/<file>@refs/tags/<tag>`, and `job_workflow_sha`
+  equals the tag commit.
+- The dispatch installation token (Actions write, Metadata read) can read
+  `GET /repos/{repo}/git/ref/tags/T` on this public repository. If the
+  repository becomes private, this needs a separate permission decision. Do not
+  silently broaden the App.
+
+If any of these does not hold, the code fails closed with an explicit code. It
+never builds with a different revision.
+
+## Recovery after `PROJECT_PREVIEW_DISPATCH_REJECT_UNRECORDED`
+
+Nothing was dispatched, but the refusal was not confirmed as recorded. The
+lease may therefore still be open. Never retry blindly.
+
+1. Read-only: check the row in `lws_internal.website_project_preview_dispatches`
+   for that `preview_lease_id` (`state`, `finished_at`, `expires_at`,
+   `workflow_run_id`). If `finished_at` is set, nothing needs doing.
+2. If it is still open, wait until `expires_at` has passed. Never edit a state
+   by hand.
+3. Read-only: list ALL unfinished expired leases
+   (`finished_at is null and expires_at <= now()`). The routine in step 4
+   processes all of them (up to 100), so the list must contain exactly the
+   expected lease(s); otherwise STOP.
+4. Only with separate owner approval: as `service_role`, run
+   `select public.expire_website_project_preview_dispatches_v1();` exactly once.
+   This existing all-dossier routine moves expired leases to FAILED with reason
+   `DEADLINE_EXCEEDED`. The scheduled cleanup covers only dossier 006 since
+   `20261108000300`.
+5. Read the row again and register the result.
+
+The stale dossier-007 lease from WP-A follows the same route.
+
+## Rollback
+
+Switching the configuration back to `refs/heads/main` is **not** a recovery. It
+only works if main at that moment equals an approved, allowlisted SHA exactly;
+otherwise the original pin-drift failure returns.
+
+- First choice: close new preview requests. Let in-flight runs finish or expire,
+  and handle them with the recovery route above.
+- Code: apply the reverse patch from the candidate package. The tag may stay;
+  it changes nothing without configuration.
+- Use the legacy main configuration only when `git rev-parse origin/main` equals
+  an allowlisted SHA exactly. Freeze main for as long as that state is needed.
